== 3. the guard on that tree, cross-checked against a SHA256SUMS

The default invocation, plus `--sha256sums`, which is what `release.yml` runs in the
`package` job: the archive digest, the digest of the bytes it decompresses to (node's own
brotli decoder, not the assembler's), the two lengths, the platform and version, and finally
the same artifact's line in `release-bins/SHA256SUMS`. The count in the OK line is packages
whose bytes were actually hashed, not packages examined.

    $ python3 scripts/ci/check-npm-integrity.py --npm-root /tmp/npm-integrity-evidence-v74ge5e9/repo/crates/codegen/xai-grok-pager/npm --sha256sums /tmp/npm-integrity-evidence-v74ge5e9/SHA256SUMS
        check-npm-integrity: OK (6 of 6 package(s) where the archive and decompressed bytes both match the record, cross-checked against SHA256SUMS)

== 4. one byte flipped in one archive

One byte at the middle of one archive. Both halves are reported: the archive no longer
hashes to the record, and the bytes it decompresses to are not the binary either. The second
finding is the one that matters for the install path -- it is what `readVerifiedBytes` stops
on -- and the guard names it without being told, because it decompresses rather than
trusting.

    $ python3 scripts/ci/check-npm-integrity.py --npm-root /tmp/npm-integrity-evidence-v74ge5e9/repo/crates/codegen/xai-grok-pager/npm --sha256sums /tmp/npm-integrity-evidence-v74ge5e9/SHA256SUMS
        check-npm-integrity: /tmp/npm-integrity-evidence-v74ge5e9/repo/crates/codegen/xai-grok-pager/npm/chaos-linux-x64/bin/chaos.br: sha256 is caacc3f0ae48b5b62d9818533bb2b4d5be6fc52a71a8f35d3b03c015cf3ad282, the record says 37fd0e9371cbd5eb41923759f9cc55a2fbc88a3bc2f084fb8bdd40bad676e9c9
        check-npm-integrity: /tmp/npm-integrity-evidence-v74ge5e9/repo/crates/codegen/xai-grok-pager/npm/chaos-linux-x64/bin/chaos.br: decompresses to bytes hashing 11e2639d2b980c7badc477af59a716a45269d744e15114ae354badfe273f9d7f, but the record calls the binary 6029bfd302856bf6ae666dbb3c4fe7e30d811f79aab854e7b6a3c63b35f4b20f; the installer hashes these same bytes and will stop on this
