        exit=1

== 5. a checkout, where nothing is assembled

A checkout, where nothing is assembled. Without `--require-assembled` that is not a failure,
because `release.yml` assembles in the `package` job and CI runs this before then; the OK
line then refuses to overstate itself and says 0 of 6. With the flag it is a refusal, which
is what `publish-npm.sh` passes when it is about to upload, so an empty or half-assembled
`npm/` tree cannot be published.

