== 6. install and launch, through the shipped entry points (linux-x64)

Everything above checks claims on disk. This drives the two programs a user runs.
`postinstall.js` writes `chaos-9.9.9` byte-identical to the release binary, links the
unversioned name to it, and replaces the package's own `bin/chaos` with a verified copy
beside the package -- which is why the entry point below runs the fixture binary with no
node in sight. Restoring the node launcher afterwards is the other half of the picture: that
is the code path taken when npm's shim or the postinstall link is not there.

