== 10. a wrong plain file of exactly the recorded length, beside a broken archive

The one place where the launcher's cheap check could have been the only check. A failed
install makes the launcher fall back to the plain file beside the archive, and the only
thing compared there is its length. A wrong file padded to exactly the recorded 53 bytes
therefore has to be stopped by the digest that failed, not survive on the strength of its
size. It is: the fall-through is guarded by the install result, and `INTEGRITY_REFUSALS` is
the set of reasons that must not fall through.

    $ stat -c '%s bytes %n' /tmp/npm-integrity-evidence-v74ge5e9/node_modules/chaos-code-linux-x64/bin/chaos
        53 bytes /tmp/npm-integrity-evidence-v74ge5e9/node_modules/chaos-code-linux-x64/bin/chaos

    $ CHAOS_HOME=/tmp/npm-integrity-evidence-v74ge5e9/home4 node node_modules/chaos-code/bin/chaos must-not-run
        chaos-code: refusing to run chaos-code-linux-x64: chaos.br (compressed) does not match bin/integrity.json
          file:     /tmp/npm-integrity-evidence-v74ge5e9/node_modules/chaos-code-linux-x64/bin/chaos.br
          expected: 37fd0e9371cbd5eb41923759f9cc55a2fbc88a3bc2f084fb8bdd40bad676e9c9
          actual:   caacc3f0ae48b5b62d9818533bb2b4d5be6fc52a71a8f35d3b03c015cf3ad282
          Re-install with `npm install -g chaos-code` after `npm cache clean --force`,
